        <div class="fsh-note" style="margin-top:10px">Why there isn\u2019t one of each every month: the Moon\u2019s orbit is tilted about 5.1\xB0 to Earth\u2019s, so most months its shadow misses. Eclipses only happen when a new or full moon lands near a node \u2014 where the two orbital planes cross. The same geometry repeats every 18 years 11\u2153 days, the Saros cycle.</div>
